# WazHack/ZX CONCEPT door (docs/design/concept-screen.md §3.1) — DRAFT for user review.
# Format = tools/gfx_convert.py --mode tile. 4 ids: arch L/R + plank L/R (planks repeat x5).
# Dim yellow $06 = wood. Open state: planks become AIR, the arch stays (no new id).
# The arch is the frame only (double stroke), so it still reads right when the door is open.
# Iron band + rivet are baked into the planks, so they repeat on every plank row.
# door_r_ring is OPTIONAL (a 5th id): a single ring handle; with only 4 ids the ring
# would repeat on all 5 plank rows, so the mock uses the plain planks.
=== door_arch_l ink:yellow paper:black
